  "description": "HUZMUL crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C82 H103 Cl3 O14 S8 Tb4,9(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb1A (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb2A (Tb) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.556-5.075 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.32-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tb4(μ4-OH)(TC4A)2Cl3(CH3OH)2(H2O)3]·9CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
